        en: 'Defects are the most measurable face of quality, so most quality programs anchor on them — but raw counts deceive twice: not all defects matter equally (data loss is not a typo), and the number reaching customers scales with install count, not just code badness. So the lesson builds the measurement chain layer by layer: severity classifies impact on an ordinal scale summarized by counts and the median; defect-removal efficiency (DRE) measures your internal nets\u2019 share of every defect that ever existed; and customer-found defects (CFD) are normalized by exposure — per thousand installs — so they measure quality, not popularity. Then we run the full loop on a hosting company called Northwind: one GQM goal translated into one customer metric, two subgoals (product and process), a real improvement — integration tests plus stronger review — and then the dangerous question: did DRE rise from 84% to 91% because the process got better, or because quarter-to-quarter luck bounces? By the end you will be able to: compute DRE and escape rate from a defect pipeline, apply CFD normalization by exposure, and read a before/after comparison with a confidence interval instead of a feeling.',
      },
    },
    {
      kind: 'predict',
      code: "before = 720\nafter = 80\nprint('caught: %d of %d' % (before, before + after))",
      question: {
        ar: 'ما حصة الشباك الداخلية من إجمالي العيوب التي وُجدت يومًا؟ وكم عيبًا أفلت إلى العملاء من كل عشرة؟ ولماذا يقيس المقام كل شيء لا الشباك وحدها؟',
        en: 'What share of all defects that ever existed did the internal nets catch? And how many of every ten escaped to customers? Why must the denominator count everything, not just the nets\u2019 catch?',
      },
      reveal: {
        ar: 'الطباعة: caught: 720 of 800. الحصة 720÷800 = 90% — أي أفلت واحد من كل عشرة، وهذا معدل الإفلات escape rate. لو كان المقام 720 وحدها لصارت النسبة 100% دائمًا مهما كثر الهاربون: كفاءة إزالة العيوب تُعرَّف D_before ÷ (D_before + D_after) × 100 لأن المقام هو كل العيوب التي وُجدت يومًا — الداخلية والهاربة معًا. و80 هنا ليست نهاية القصة: الأنبوب الجاري في هذا الفصل يقيّمها إصدارًا بعد إصدار.',
        en: 'It prints caught: 720 of 800. The share is 720/800 = 90% — one of every ten escaped, and that is the escape rate. With a denominator of 720 alone the ratio would be 100% forever no matter how many escaped: DRE is defined as D_before / (D_before + D_after) x 100 because the denominator is every defect that ever existed — internal catches plus escapes. And the 80 is not the end of the story: the pipeline in this lesson\u2019s exercise grades it release by release.',
