        en: 'Four lines summarize the whole product metric: D_before = 720 is what your nets swept before shipping (review + static analysis + testing), D_after = 80 what customers found in six months. The formula lives in line three: 100.0 x 720 / 800 = 90.0 — note multiplying by the float 100.0 before dividing so the ratio never collapses. The escape rate on line four is the complementary face: 100 - DRE = 10% — the fraction that got through. Two faces of one coin, but DRE is the one you set as a target (95% is a common aspiration) because raising it means inflating your finds alone is not enough — real escapes must fall. And the last caution: this value stays provisional until the six-month window closes; customer defect number 81 may arrive tomorrow.',
