        en: 'A two-release pipeline (releases is given): each release holds before (removed by your internal nets) and prod (found by customers). Inside the loop: compute the release\u2019s DRE and print it as %s DRE: %.1f%%, and accumulate before into sum_before and prod into sum_prod (both pre-defined). After the loop the print is already written: pooled escape: %.1f%% — the pooled escape rate = 100 x sum of prod / (sum of before + sum of prod). Expected: r1 DRE: 90.0%, then r2 DRE: 93.0%, then pooled escape: 8.8%.',
      },
      starterCode: "releases = {'r1': {'before': 720, 'prod': 80}, 'r2': {'before': 465, 'prod': 35}}\nsum_before = 0\nsum_prod = 0\n\nfor k in releases:\n    d = releases[k]\n    # احسب DRE وأطبعه، وجمع القيم في sum_before وsum_prod\n    # compute and print DRE; accumulate sum_before and sum_prod\n    pass\n\nescape = 100.0 * sum_prod / (sum_before + sum_prod)\nprint('pooled escape: %.1f%%' % escape)",
      solution: "releases = {'r1': {'before': 720, 'prod': 80}, 'r2': {'before': 465, 'prod': 35}}\nsum_before = 0\nsum_prod = 0\nfor k in releases:\n    d = releases[k]\n    dre = 100.0 * d['before'] / (d['before'] + d['prod'])\n    print('%s DRE: %.1f%%' % (k, dre))\n    sum_before += d['before']\n    sum_prod += d['prod']\nescape = 100.0 * sum_prod / (sum_before + sum_prod)\nprint('pooled escape: %.1f%%' % escape)",
