      kind: 'sandbox',
      starterCode: "releases = {'r1': {'before': 720, 'prod': 80}, 'r2': {'before': 465, 'prod': 35}}\nsum_before = 0\nsum_prod = 0\nfor k in releases:\n    d = releases[k]\n    dre = 100.0 * d['before'] / (d['before'] + d['prod'])\n    print('%s DRE: %.1f%%' % (k, dre))\n    sum_before += d['before']\n    sum_prod += d['prod']\nescape = 100.0 * sum_prod / (sum_before + sum_prod)\nprint('pooled escape: %.1f%%' % escape)\n\ninstalls = {'r1': 200, 'r2': 5000}\nfor k in releases:\n    print('%s CFD per 1k installs: %.2f' % (k, 1000.0 * releases[k]['prod'] / installs[k]))\n\n# جرّب: ضاعف تنصيبتات r1 خمس مرات وأعد الحساب — أي سطر تغيّر وأي سطر ثابت؟\n# try: quintuple r1's installs and recompute — which line moved and which stayed?\n# جرّب: أزل التطبيع واقرأ العمودين كجودة — أي نسخة تخدع؟\n# try: drop the normalization and read the two columns as quality — which version lies?\n# جرّب: أضف r3 بـbefore = 0 — ماذا يفعل المقام الصفري بصيغة DRE؟ متى تنفجر الصيغة؟\n# try: add r3 with before = 0 — what does a zero numerator do to DRE? when does the formula blow up?",
